## Whole-day delay per test day (mean over replications) and twin capacity check

Capacity check: GDOT's PM plan C gives Piedmont-from-N through (P8, 2 lanes) 48.4 s of green per 180 s. 'Implied saturation flow' = the discharge rate per lane of green needed to pass that day's counted PM peak hour. Above 2000 veh/h/lane it is physically implausible, i.e. the counts and plan C don't fit together in the twin (GDOT's detectors did count those vehicles), and the real-timing number for that day reflects the twin/counts, not GDOT's controller.

